n Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T09:08:53-07:00","id":1103517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103516#post1103516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I thought non-backers got a chance to see books during the errata collection part?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol nope...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T09:15:14-07:00","id":1103520,"title":"","content":"The V20 Dark Ages Companion is up on DTRPG as an advanced version for errata collection, why wouldn't BoS? Or like I asked, is there a step before that too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T09:40:32-07:00","id":1103530,"title":"","content":"I express my condolences to the non-backers, whose M20 books do not contain the Correct Paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T10:23:26-07:00","id":1103543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrackedMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103520#post1103520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The V20 Dark Ages Companion is up on DTRPG as an advanced version for errata collection, why wouldn't BoS? Or like I asked, is there a step before that too?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, our PDFs come out on one of two tracks: Advance PDFs that folks buy and then send in any errata, and Backer PDFs that go to KS backers as part of their rewards (usually from Stretch Goals) before the material goes on sale to the public. The V20 DA Companion is not a Stretch Goal reward, but BoS is. So backers get to peruse the PDF and help us with errata before it goes up on sale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T10:31:38-07:00","id":1103544,"title":"","content":"Ah, ok! That makes more sense, thank you for the clarification. Totally a bummer for me, but nothing to be done about that now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1885-crackedman","name":"CrackedMan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1885_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T11:25:20-07:00","id":1103556,"title":"","content":"I'm particularly enjoying all the new merits and flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T12:31:42-07:00","id":1103581,"title":"","content":"They've apparently gone the route of <b> Forged by Dragon's Fire</b> and overcomplicated the categorization of Wonders by treating the technologies as something distinct from the non-technological Wonders. Why not say \u201cArtifacts, Charms, Fetishes, Grimoires, Periapts, Primers, Relics, Talismans, and Trinkets\u201d, and then briefly mention somewhere that the Technocracy tends to use its own terminology (Devices instead of Talismans, Gadgets instead of Charms, Inventions instead of Artifacts, Matrices instead of Periapts, Principae instead of Grimoires) and leave it at that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-14-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:50:25-07:00","id":1103601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103581#post1103581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've apparently gone the route of <b> Forged by Dragon's Fire</b> and overcomplicated the categorization of Wonders by treating the technologies as something distinct from the non-technological Wonders. Why not say \u201cArtifacts, Charms, Fetishes, Grimoires, Periapts, Primers, Relics, Talismans, and Trinkets\u201d, and then briefly mention somewhere that the Technocracy tends to use its own terminology (Devices instead of Talismans, Gadgets instead of Charms, Inventions instead of Artifacts, Matrices instead of Periapts, Principae instead of Grimoires) and leave it at that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idk, maybe toss it up in the errata thread and see what sticks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T15:45:21-07:00","id":1103635,"title":"","content":".... Does Hands of Daedalus basically allow you to have all the advantages of Personalized and nonpersonalized instruments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T16:24:33-07:00","id":1103645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103581#post1103581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've apparently gone the route of <b> Forged by Dragon's Fire</b> and overcomplicated the categorization of Wonders by treating the technologies as something distinct from the non-technological Wonders. Why not say \u201cArtifacts, Charms, Fetishes, Grimoires, Periapts, Primers, Relics, Talismans, and Trinkets\u201d, and then briefly mention somewhere that the Technocracy tends to use its own terminology (Devices instead of Talismans, Gadgets instead of Charms, Inventions instead of Artifacts, Matrices instead of Periapts, Principae instead of Grimoires) and leave it at that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Devices are actually a seperate thing entirely with different rules for crafting them? Or if that's no longer the case, vestigial organs from past editions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T18:28:26-07:00","id":1103678,"title":"","content":"Going back and skimming that section over, there do seem to be at least some rules variations for the techno-Wonders, not all mechanical. The differences are minor, and perhaps in a vacuum things would be better if the differences were more standardized (like dropping Instruments), but between M20 still being a legacy product, and feeling the diversity of magical items as being beneficial complexity more than not for players to buy/make the Wonders that most suit what they're trying to do, I think it's fine.<br /> <br /> I think there's way more questionable word count in having even more Secondary Abilities printed up (or if this was going to be the case as M20 core and the three main 'stuff we couldn't fit in' books, why not move all the Secondary Abilities to BoS?), and the FAQ... not really being that useful. Like, there are some very useful entries, and ones that I would find useful things to address some long standing Internet debates (the one on Mage not really being liberal or conservative, and trying to put the game's political themes in those categories isn't really the point), but way too many of the answers come down to, &quot;it was my editorial choice,&quot; without that much real useful insight into how to handle those choices if we don't like them besides being pointed to Rule Zero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T18:44:31-07:00","id":1103680,"title":"","content":"Were we supposed to get more information on some of the name dropped factions like the Mirainohmen or am I misremembering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T19:46:35-07:00","id":1103694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026#post1103464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026a <b>Book of Secrets</b>, actually. I'm downloading from DTRPG as I write this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't lie - I saw the title from the main list, and couldn't help but find it funny if the next words were that you were the modern man, with parts made in Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T20:26:46-07:00","id":1103700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103680#post1103680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were we supposed to get more information on some of the name dropped factions like the Mirainohmen or am I misremembering?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the third supplement of things that didn't make it into M20 Core?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T00:45:29-07:00","id":1103745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103700#post1103700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that was the third supplement of things that didn't make it into M20 Core?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It doesn't look like it will be in the Character pack, Nephandi or techno book..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T01:01:12-07:00","id":1103746,"title":"","content":"Gods, Monsters, and other Familiar Strangers is the only announced book that makes any sense to expand on them via sample characters. Otherwise it would have to be in some not yet announced M20 version of the Book of Crafts which would further delve into the Disparate Alliance like the new Technocracy book is going to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T03:43:11-07:00","id":1103762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103746#post1103746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gods, Monsters, and other Familiar Strangers is the only announced book that makes any sense to expand on them via sample characters. Otherwise it would have to be in some not yet announced M20 version of the Book of Crafts which would further delve into the Disparate Alliance like the new Technocracy book is going to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is not on the list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T15:54:43-07:00","id":1103994,"title":"","content":"While i appreciate the rules on resonance and the Flaws &amp; Merits that were missing in M20 Core, there is too much i dont like in this book<br /> <br /> 1) As always Brucatto\u00b4s ego shines through in the worst possible way. From wasting wordcount into bragging how he is fit for his old age to covering his ass in the most &quot;i am not racist, i have A black friend&quot; way possible. From wasting word count on the &quot;Neurodiversity and mental traits&quot; side bars to a paragraph on why he change the name of the flaw &quot;lame&quot;. It wasnt needed or it could be all be put on 1 paragraph on the FAQ.<br /> <br /> 2) The FAQ, this is both Brucatto hiding behind the &quot;i was young at the time&quot; or &quot;others did it&quot; excuse time and time again. Or posing question that nobody asked or doing the ones people have asked but not answering the point of the question. I specially &quot;love&quot; the &quot;Why mage is so liberal&quot; question that he smugly answered &quot;forgetting&quot; than in truth the question is &quot;Why M20, a game with so little word count that it needed 3 books waste word count in stroking the authors ego and political leaning for him to tell us that we should eat organic?&quot; <br /> <br /> Also the question of the Disparate, whose answer is &quot;meh WW2 axis, weirdest things have happened&quot;. Yeah no, thats not an explanation. I dont mind the concept of disparate and yes, WW2 was a chaotic time but it really REALLY didn't happened in 1 day and thats the problem with them. We are getting this new faction of very unlikely allies that band together for reasons and we dont get a satisfactory story about them. Honestly they could just make it a stretch goal to make the Guide to Disparates and explain better the history and alliance.<br /> <br /> 3) Secondary abilities some really blend to much with other others are so specific as to not be worthy of being secondary skills. And it just seems like a XP sink. Those that are relevant could be just be in the Core on the first place.<br /> <br /> 4) Focus and paradigm section is fine though the whole over-cluttering of paradigm is a problem in M20 trying to shove to many decisions on a new PC beforehand. It could have used a trimming in both book and should have been in the Core. <br /> <br /> 5) The expanded rule section is fine though i haven't delved to deep in them to see if they break the system anymore than M20 already did. Child mage rules are a waste of word-count and i sorely miss the Specialty sphere optional rules. Though there are rules that again, should have been in the Core like internet and Resonance. <br /> <br /> 6) Page 272 to 298 is a complete and utter unprofessional waste of word-count and the book even acknowledges it calling it Restless Rambles. I dont need Brucato bare-bones definition of genres and while the recommendations of books are fine it could have being done in 2 pages.<br /> <br /> The fact that this books contains so many necesary rules is the worst part considering that M20 could have cut a lot of its material and or shove some of their most unimportant one in this one.<br /> <br /> The disparates (28 pages) should have been in the Book of secrets. Chapter 7 (42 pages) is unimportant and should have been either in the book of secret of entirely cut off. The whole paradigm and Focus section on M20 didn't need to be on 2 different chapter and sure as hell could have use a trimming.<br /> <br /> And as the title of one of the sections said &quot;Restless ramblings&quot; is the biggest problem with M20. Brucatto apparently is not a professional capable of being given free reign on a book any halfway decent editor could and should have cut his useless ramblings away. He is more concerned on wax about how great he is and how good mage was than actually delivering a good product and thats not getting into the fact everything good that Mage is was done by other people grabbing his concept and making it worthwhile. As the some people say, he is the Rob Liefeld to his mage\u00b4s Deadpool and the existence of this book along with M20 is the ultimate proof of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T16:27:20-07:00","id":1104012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1103994#post1103994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Whole lot of truth.</div> </div> </div> </div> Man the guy knows how to pad a book, what's he get paid by the word?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T19:01:51-07:00","id":1104097,"title":"","content":"I thought the paradigm/practice examples were very helpful, though I thought it was pretty funny that almost every sample character had more than seven instruments.<br /> <br /> I also liked the child mage section. I always find it useful to see how different writers will tackle these kind of variations on the standard character types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-15-2017, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T20:34:01-07:00","id":1104135,"title":"","content":"From the FAQ:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Why Didn\u2019t You Detail the \u201cCamps\u201d \u2013 </b><b>That is, Groups Within Each Tradition, </b><b>Technocratic Methodologies, and So On? </b></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">I tried. But between the two-page spread limit, the sheer number of those smaller groups (the Order of Hermes alone has 13 Houses and a number of smaller fellowships!), and the need for at least 200-300 words per group in order to describe a \u201ccamp\u201d with any degree of detail, there was just no way to fit that material into Mage 20\u2026 or, for that matter, into the book in your hands right now, which was originally supposed <br /> to contain that material until I added up the words and realized it wasn\u2019t going to fit. <br /> <br /> As of this writing, the plan is to put that material into a book dedicated specifically to the \u201ccamps.\u201d That project has not yet been approved or scheduled, however, so the best response I can give right now is \u201cWe plan to get it out there eventually.\u201d</div> <br /> My advice: give up on trying to fit it all into a single book. Give us the Nephandic factions in <b>Book of the Fallen</b>, the Technocratic factions in <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b>, the Traditional factions in a Traditions-centered counterpart, the Disparate factions in a Disparates-oriented book, and the Marauder \u201cfactions\u201d (such as they are) in an M20 Book of Madness. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T08:26:25-07:00","id":1104302,"title":"","content":"My advice: fire Brucatto from any other M20 project. Or heavily limit his involvement and get a editor to triple check what he writes and make the proper cuts. Like <br /> <br /> &quot;Look Phil, nobody cares about that you have RL &quot;experience&quot; on occultism or that you believe that playing Nephandi is gonna make you one or even that you believe gamers should eat organic small local food. Or if they care, they dont care to read it on the book. Its nice and everything but save that for your blog/facebook page and the poor souls that still follows that. So we gonna cut those from the book and you, young man, will go and think on proper mechanics for magic and decent backstory for the Disparates&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-16-2017, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T09:44:53-07:00","id":1104339,"title":"","content":"I admit, I am not too concerned with the &quot;camps&quot; since we still have the old tradition books for those. I would love to see more future fates type information on how modern events may have impacted the major groups.<br /> <br /> So far, they've been focused a lot on the Reckoning plot, understandably, but I would love to see more in the vein of Threat Null, the Nephandi infiltration, and the Disparate Alliance (I love that idea especially as a means to open up more possibilities for players who are understandably tired of the Eurocentric focus of the Traditions.)<br /> <br /> Really, I think I'd love a giant &quot;metaplot&quot; type book that we could use or discard elements of at will. I am probably the only one in that boat though. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T12:57:50-07:00","id":1104434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104302#post1104302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice: fire Brucatto from any other M20 project. Or heavily limit his involvement and get a editor to triple check what he writes and make the proper cuts. Like</div> </div> </div> </div>And my advice would be:<br /> Consider that there are enough players who don't want their books to be simply dry writing and listings of rules, and might enjoy his style. I do.<br /> <br /> While I'd say that, yes, there are certainly parts that are too wordy (The resonance chapter comes to mind - that one somewhat grinds my gears in how it dances around the explanation of the concepts over and over...), and unnecessary (Many of the secondary abilities which are just specialties of normal abilites) I very much enjoy that he likes to give lots of examples, cross-references between parts of the book, suggests use cases, explains possible motivations and consequences (Both positive and negative) of certain actions and character types, uses RL examples, and finally actually answers a few speculations and 'Why did he' questions pulled form forums and Facebook, unlike other authors that remain completely silent.<br /> <br /> So, all in all I really liked the book, even if there are some parts that I thought were unnecessary or too wordy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:43:41-07:00","id":1104464,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104434#post1104434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my advice would be:<br /> Consider that there are enough players who don't want their books to be simply dry writing and listings of rules, and might enjoy his style. I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all the rules were covered already in the book and then he got 20 or 50 pages completely free then sure. But he went on and on about how he needed 2 more books aside from the Core to fit all of M20 and then i gotta read things like Brucattos idea of &quot;gamer should eat local produced food&quot; then those ramblings should have been the first ones to get cut not the rules.<br /> <br /> If wordcount is an issue then reading 4 times that X element was changed because &quot;he was a ignorant teenager and didnt had the access to information we got today when he wrote X&quot; reek of unprofessionalism.<br /> <br /> M20 should have contained all the nescesary rules and Book of secrets should have contained the Disparates and all the mad rambling he wanted to fit in there.<br /> <br /> I read in 4chan a few months ago of an anon doing a &quot;Brucatto bullshit free&quot; fan edition of M20 and sincerily hope that anon godspeed because we need a good M20 edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104434#post1104434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">finally actually answers a few speculations and 'Why did he' questions pulled form forums and Facebook, unlike other authors that remain completely silent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that the book is not the place to answer those questions. He could just make a post in the OPP page and said &quot;this why i did X&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:48:18-07:00","id":1104467,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say I like Saytros' editorial writing style, but it doesn't bother me too much either. I think he's one of the few people that is really good at capturing what Mage is supposed to be about, and can bridge the different edition's variations very well. So firing him or limiting him would be a huge mistake in my mind.<br /> <br /> The most I would think could be good for the game is someone a bit more focused on the &quot;making sure this is valuable to people in play, and isn't redundant&quot; was working with him to balance out the creative team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T13:58:36-07:00","id":1104472,"title":"","content":"I like Brucato's style overall. I tend to think a lot of the wordiness may simply be the result of a decade's worth of pent up thoughts and speculation on the subject. I thought the FAQ was a bit much, but to be fair to him, he was answering legitimate questions and conversation topics that we've seen on this forum and others.<br /> <br /> I suspect that now that he's gotten a lot of this out of his system, we'll see fewer digressions in later books. But even if I'm wrong, I can't say I'm too bothered. I didn't pay for the book by the word after all. <br /> <br /> I've found Mage 20 to be as playable as the any of the editions that came before and I've appreciated the practicality of most of the rule changes. So I'm pretty happy with things as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T14:04:03-07:00","id":1104475,"title":"","content":"I do think that a \u201cdesigner's notes\u201d blog entry would have been a better place for much of what ended up in the FAQ, and that advice for what the reader should do in his or her personal life should have been first on the chopping block. That is, I'm sympathetic to LokiRavenSpeak's concerns: I fear we're getting the Lucas Effect, where a developer who was central to the creation of a beloved project is given free rein on its revival; and because there's no one who can credibly tell him no, he goes overboard. I don't think he needs to be fired; but I do wish his editors would do a better job of tightening up the text and keeping him on point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T15:52:55-07:00","id":1104510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104464#post1104464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that the book is not the place to answer those questions. He could just make a post in the OPP page and said &quot;this why i did X&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104475#post1104475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that a \u201cdesigner's notes\u201d blog entry would have been a better place for much of what ended up in the FAQ,</div> </div> </div> </div>See, here's the thing about that...<br /> I don't do facebook, or like to browse through blog posts to find official answers for things. There have been, from what I heard, a lot of FAQ-style online posts even back in the original WW days about some of their books, decisions and rules. I think Just John mentioned something along those lines multiple times.<br /> <br /> The funny thing is, we still have those books from those days, but finding those posts is next to impossible.<br /> An online FAQ for current books works fine *right now*. But sites vanish. get moved, posts get wiped or simply lost in the belly of the internet over the years. The books remain, so if I can find the questions and answers I want about the books, while holding said books, no matter if it's now or in five years or ten, that's a big bonus for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 06-16-2017, 06:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T15:59:27-07:00","id":1104513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104510#post1104510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The funny thing is, we still have those books from those days, but finding those posts is next to impossible. An online FAQ for current books *right now* works fine. But.<br /> Sites vanish. get moved, posts get wiped or simply lost in the belly of the internet over the years. The books remain, so if I can find the questions and answers I want about the books, while holding said books, no matter if it's now or in five years or ten, that's a big bonus for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then isnt now. We got wayback machine and there is plenty of ways now to make that document not be lost. For example put it up a as a free PDF on Drivethru or the page we are in like OPP has done in the past. So far your only argument is that you like the unproffesionalism of Brucatto because you are too lazy to check a webpage which you currently in.<br /> <br /> Besides as a PDF it could be edited so it could contain even MORE Brucatto ramblings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-16-2017, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:15:14-07:00","id":1104520,"title":"","content":"Wow, that seems unnecessarily insulting and dismissive. Many of these questions have come up repeatedly in some form or another since 2003. And there are fans who value having at least semi-official answers in an easily accessible format. Not every fan accesses the forums, nor wants to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:26:59-07:00","id":1104525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104520#post1104520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, that seems unnecessarily insulting and dismissive. Many of these questions have come up repeatedly in some form or another since 2003. And there are fans who value having at least semi-official answers in an easily accessible format. Not every fan accesses the forums, nor wants to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those same fan can order a pdf or pod from drivethru but wouldnt be able to access drivethru, the opp main page, the forums or just simple google to get the FAQ?<br /> <br /> Also is kind of a cheap money grab that those fan have to pay, because not all people got into the kickstarter for a pdf/book to get an answer to the questions raised in the Core they already bought.<br /> <br /> Since 2003? You are talking about the design choices or the rules clarifications for M20 part of the FAQ? Because if it is the former then your argument got even less of a leg to stand. Why Brucatto did what it did is anecdotical at best. And doesnt have a place in a rulebook","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:36:16-07:00","id":1104529,"title":"","content":"Thus \u201cfree PDF on DTRPG\u201d. But yeah; could you please tone down the insults, LokiRavenSpeak?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:42:25-07:00","id":1104530,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I would consider myself probably as far into the strike zone of Mage's ostensible politics as it is possible to be, and I <i>still </i>find Brucato's self-mythologizing and editorializing off-putting. Not for its existence but, frankly, for its immaturity and its occasional philosophical incoherence. I don't want a dry, scholarly tome, but I wouldn't mind one that didn't provoke so much cringing embarrassment. Brucato imagines Mage as a vehicle for educating his readership and provoking them to action - which would be fine, if if his assessment of our knowledge and our character wasn't so... <i>limited</i>. I don't mind the occasional lecture - but only if the lecturer knows what the hell they're talking about.<br /> <br /> It would be hard for me to find words to explain how irksome, how <i>alienating </i>I find M20 to be, after two decades as a fan, player, and storyteller. Should its trajectory set the tone for what is to come, Book of Secrets is probably going to mark the point where I begin to transition from fan to ex-fan. I don't think this is because I have never grasped the True Heart of the game. I think it's because Brucato's Mage is such a personal project that M20 is caught up in the eddies of his preferences (and <i>biases</i>) - which means stripping away the good work that other writers have done in the sandbox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i> I attack people with giant insects both </i>on <i>and </i>off <i>the court.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1653-five-eyes","name":"Five Eyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"395"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:43:39-07:00","id":1104531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104525#post1104525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those same fan can order a pdf or pod from drivethru but wouldnt be able to access drivethru, the opp main page, the forums or just simple google to get the FAQ?<br /> <br /> Also is kind of a cheap money grab that those fan have to pay, because not all people got into the kickstarter for a pdf/book to get an answer to the questions raised in the Core they already bought.<br /> <br /> Since 2003? You are talking about the design choices or the rules clarifications for M20 part of the FAQ? Because if it is the former then your argument got even less of a leg to stand. Why Brucatto did what it did is anecdotical at best. And doesnt have a place in a rulebook</div> </div> </div> </div>There are questions in the FAQ that date back farther than M20, though many of the questions are M20 specific. Questions like the &quot;what happens when a mage is embraced&quot; for example, or certain of the metaplot questions.<br /> <br /> But yes, there are fans who took part in the Kickstarter, who also purchase through DriveThruRPG who don't go to these forums. Certain attitudes (such as dismissive accusations that people who have different opinions are &quot;lazy&quot;) might well be a part of that, too. Some of us, myself included, only come to these forums periodically. We're more than capable of being loyal and devoted fans without it.<br /> <br /> Other fans may not be inclined to search through thirty pages of forum to get answers to their questions (have you tried using the search function to find specific information here? It can be a considerable slog.) Some folks also would like to get &quot;official&quot; answers to their questions. Brucato doesn't post here, to my knowledge anyway. And not everyone knows about his facebook page. Which, by the way, is even harder to navigate. And some folks aren't comfortable asking questions directly in a public format. A separate FAQ would be fine too, but I don't see why it's such a bad thing that it's part of the Book of Secrets either.<br /> <br /> Besides, FAQs have been a common part of Storyteller Guides for a long time (see for example, Book of Mirrors.). Sometimes they're useful, sometimes they're not. Personally though, I like being able to look things up in the actual books, which I can use even when I don't have access to the Internet. So I'm happy about most of the FAQ, and the rest? I skip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-16-2017, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:46:59-07:00","id":1104532,"title":"","content":"I just finished reading the book and I must confess it has left a bittersweet taste in my mouth. The chapters inside the book feel disconnected from one another as if someone had put together a document with the missing pieces of several other documents, which is exactly what happened when you think about it.<br /> However, as for the new information presented in the book I have to say that I liked it. I always welcome more options to personalize my game, and from that point of view, I believe that the book of secrets delivers.<br /> Its true Satyros tone can be a bit preachy sometimes, but I really like his style. I may be in the minority, but I believe that the liberal tendencies that people say are in the book are not as present as they proclaim. As always, it's a matter of opinion, but for me, the book maintains an acceptable professional tone in the majority of its pages.<br /> I believe that the main problem with the latest edition of mage comes from Satyros doing too much on his own. It's too much work for one single person, regardless of how much that person is familiar with the source material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 07-26-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:58:11-07:00","id":1104536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1103464-i-have-a-secret\u2026?p=1104302#post1104302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My advice: fire Brucatto from any other M20 